# A lowercase widget of another module written qualified, `@Parts.header`: applied as a
# line of a block, and read as a blueprint value (Semantics ch. 6: every declaration of
# a module is reachable by its qualified name, written `@Birds.Spotter`, the sigil
# before the module's name, and "a qualified name is one token"; Jimmy's ruling QN: a
# qualified name needs no `use`; ch. 8: a blueprint builds where a block applies it).
# sem-ch06-qualified-lowercase with a widget for the `let`. Written by Claude on the
# claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Parts
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

?Pick: fn Bool, @a -> ?@a
fn ?Pick b, @w = if b: ? @w else: nil

@page: @unit
@page:
    @Parts.header                                                # 0
    match ?Pick True, @Parts.header:                             # 1
        ? @t: @t
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"none")
    Ui.Label($text=$"end")                                       # 2
